# Documents, fragments, commands, and streams

**Prerequisites:** [first app](/docs/tutorials/first-app/).
**Kind:** concept.
**Next:** [Update the UI](/docs/how-to/update-the-ui/) or
[Runtime](/docs/reference/runtime/).

Rocci treats HTML as the shared boundary. JavaScript enhances; it is not the
unit of composition.

| Handler | Typical result | Browser behavior |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `@view` | Complete HTML document | Load or navigate |
| `@patch` | Fragment with a stable target | One-shot morph in the acting tab |
| `@command` | Roc data | **empty SSE** when `Datastar-Request: true`; else JSON |
| `@live` | Shared fragment | Generated `GET /sse`; every open tab morphs |

`@live` does not replace `@view` or `@patch`. Do not patch the same `id` from
both a `@command` and the stream.

Canonical comparison: [Counter](/examples/counter/) versus
[Live counter](/examples/live-counter/).

**Related:** [Datastar as transport](/docs/concepts/datastar-as-transport/).
